tom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; letter-spacing=
: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">Total revenue was $11,439&nbsp;million, an=
 increase of $880&nbsp;million or&nbsp;8% from the prior year. Net interest=
 income increased $809&nbsp;million or&nbsp;10%, due to higher balances and=
 net interest margins. Non-interest revenue increased $71&nbsp;million or&n=
bsp;3%, primarily due to the inclusion of AIR MILES, higher mutual fund dis=
tribution fee revenue and card-related revenue, partially offset by lower c=
ommercial lending fee revenue. Net interest margin of&nbsp;2.77% increased&=
nbsp;5&nbsp;basis points from the prior year, due to higher loan margins an=
d deposits growing faster than loans, partially offset by lower deposit mar=
gins. The impact of the transition of bankers=E2=80=99 acceptances exposure=
s to loans in Commercial Banking resulted in lower non-interest revenue off=
set in net interest income, with a modest reduction in the net interest mar=
gin. </div></div><div style=3D"text-indent: 4%; font-family: arial; font-si=
ze: 8pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"font-family: a=
rial; font-size: 8pt; letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">Person=
al and Business Banking revenue increased $694&nbsp;million or&nbsp;9%, due=
 to higher net interest income and non-interest revenue. Commercial Banking=
 revenue increased $186&nbsp;million or&nbsp;6%, due to higher net interest=
 income, partially offset by lower non-interest revenue. </div></div><div s=
tyle=3D"text-indent: 4%; font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; margin-top: 0p=
