etter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">Total provision for credit lo=
sses was $1,659&nbsp;million, an increase of $750&nbsp;million from the pri=
or year. The provision for credit losses on impaired loans was&nbsp;$1,326&=
nbsp;million, an increase of $602&nbsp;million from the prior year, reflect=
ing higher provisions in Personal and Business Banking, driven by unsecured=
 segments of the consumer portfolio, and Commercial Banking. There was a $3=
33&nbsp;million provision for credit losses on performing loans in the curr=
ent year, compared with a $185&nbsp;million provision in the prior year. </=
div></div><div style=3D"text-indent: 4%; font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt=
