wer interest rates and expansionary fiscal policies, including a possible r=
eduction in the corporate tax rate. The Federal Reserve lowered its key len=
ding rate for the first time in four years in September&nbsp;2024 by&nbsp;5=
0 basis points and will likely continue to reduce rates in 2025. As a resul=
t, business and consumer lending demand is expected to improve through&nbsp=
;fiscal 2025 while deposit costs should stabilize. The lower cost of borrow=
ing is expected to ease pressure on household and business balance sheets. =
</div></div><div style=3D"text-indent: 4%; font-family: arial; font-size: 8=
