e;">Financial Review </div></div></div></div><div style=3D"font-family: ari=
al; font-size: 8pt; margin-top: 4pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">BMO Wealth Manage=
ment reported results reflected the adoption of IFRS&nbsp;17, <div style=3D=
"font-style: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;"><div st=
yle=3D"font-style:italic;display:inline;">Insurance Contracts </div></div>(=
IFRS&nbsp;17), effective November&nbsp;1,&nbsp;2023. IFRS&nbsp;17 provides =
a comprehensive approach to accounting for all types of insurance contracts=
 and replaced IFRS&nbsp;4, <div style=3D"font-style: normal; letter-spacing=
: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;"><div style=3D"font-style:italic;display:in=
line;">Insurance Contracts. </div></div>Insurance results are now presented=
 in non-interest revenue under insurance service results and insurance inve=
stment results. As a result of the adoption and retrospective application o=
f IFRS&nbsp;17 to our fiscal&nbsp;2023 results, we no longer report insuran=
ce claims, commissions and changes in policy benefit liabilities. For furth=
er details, refer to Note&nbsp;1 of the audited annual consolidated financi=
al statements. </div><div style=3D"font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; marg=
in-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"font-family: arial; font-si=
ze: 8pt; letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">Reported net income=
 was $1,248&nbsp;million, an increase of $102&nbsp;million or&nbsp;9% from =
the prior year. Wealth and Asset Management reported net income was $1,012&=
nbsp;million, an increase of $188&nbsp;million or&nbsp;23%, and included on=
e additional quarter of Bank of the West results, compared with the prior y=
ear. Insurance net income was $236&nbsp;million, a decrease of $86&nbsp;mil=
lion or&nbsp;27%. </div></div><div style=3D"text-indent: 4%; font-family: a=
rial; font-size: 8pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"f=
ont-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:in=
line;">Total revenue was $5,646&nbsp;million, an increase of $235&nbsp;mill=
ion or&nbsp;4%. Revenue in Wealth and Asset Management was $5,279&nbsp;mill=
ion, an increase of $349&nbsp;million or&nbsp;7%, due to growth in client a=
ssets, including the impact of stronger global markets, and higher revenue =
from online brokerage transactions, partially offset by lower net interest =
income due to lower margins. Insurance revenue was $367&nbsp;million, a dec=
rease of $114&nbsp;million, reflecting changes in portfolio positioning dur=
ing the transition to IFRS&nbsp;17. </div></div><div style=3D"text-indent: =
4%; font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt=
;"><div style=3D"font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; letter-spacing: 0px; t=
op: 0px;display:inline;">The total provision for credit losses was $31&nbsp=
;million, compared with an $18&nbsp;million provision in the prior year. Th=
e provision for credit losses on impaired loans increased $21&nbsp;million =
and the provision for credit losses on performing loans decreased $8&nbsp;m=
illion. </div></div><div style=3D"text-indent: 4%; font-family: arial; font=
-size: 8pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"font-family=
: arial; font-size: 8pt; letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">Non=
-interest expense was $3,968&nbsp;million, an increase of $90&nbsp;million =
or&nbsp;2% from the prior year, due to higher revenue-based costs and our i=
nvestment in talent, partially offset by operational efficiencies. </div></=
div><div style=3D"text-indent: 4%; font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; marg=
in-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"font-family: arial; font-si=
ze: 8pt; letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">Assets under manage=
ment increased $89.8&nbsp;billion or&nbsp;27% from the prior year to $422.7=
&nbsp;billion, driven by stronger global markets and higher net client asse=
ts. Assets under administration decreased $55.1&nbsp;billion or&nbsp;13% to=
&nbsp;$361.2&nbsp;billion, primarily due to the exit of our Institutional T=
rust Services operations in the first quarter of fiscal 2024, partially off=
set by stronger global markets. Average gross loans increased&nbsp;5% and a=
verage deposits were relatively unchanged from the prior year. </div></div>=
<div style=3D"text-indent: 4%; font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; margin-t=
op: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">For further information on non-GAAP amounts, =
measures and ratios in this 2024 Operating Groups Performance Review sectio=
n, refer to the <div style=3D"white-space: nowrap; letter-spacing: 0px; top=
: 0px;display:inline;">Non-GAAP</div> and Other Financial Measures section.=
 </div><div style=3D"font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"=
><div style=3D"font-size: 12pt; letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inlin=
e;">&nbsp;</div></div><div style=3D"line-height: 1pt; margin-top: 0pt; marg=
in-bottom: 2pt; border-bottom-color: rgb(34, 92, 171); border-bottom-width:=
 1px; border-bottom-style: solid;"><div style=3D"letter-spacing: 0px; top: =
0px;display:inline;">&nbsp;</div></div><div style=3D"font-family: arial; fo=
nt-size: 14pt; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"color: r=
gb(34, 92, 171); letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;"><div style=
=3D"letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;"><div style=3D"font-weigh=
t:bold;display:inline;">Business Environment and Outlook </div></div></div>=
</div><div style=3D"font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; margin-top: 4pt; ma=
rgin-bottom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; letter=
-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">BMO Wealth Management results bene=
fitted from growing momentum in equity markets through fiscal 2024, with a =
moderation of inflationary pressures and declining interest rates in the se=
cond half of the year. Higher assets under management from stronger global =
markets and net new asset flows supported revenue growth, offsetting the in=
dustry-wide reduction in asset yields and lower net interest margins from d=
eposit migration to higher yielding assets. We continue to invest in techno=
logy platforms to simplify, streamline and integrate digital solutions for =
our clients, along with advisor-facing tools. BMO Global Asset Management a=
