 advancing our strategic priorities. The operating environment in fiscal&nb=
sp;2024 was impacted by challenging global economic trends and growing geop=
olitical risks. Despite these market dynamics, we saw improved issuance act=
ivity and robust trading results driven by strong client flows; however, me=
rgers and acquisitions activity, particularly in Canada, remained muted. </=
div></div><div style=3D"text-indent: 4%; font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt=
; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"font-family: arial; f=
ont-size: 8pt; letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">In fiscal&nbs=
p;2025, we expect market volatility to persist through an uncertain economi=
c outlook. Advisory and debt issuance activity is expected to improve in a =
lower interest rate environment, and the trading landscape will likely be c=
haracterized by enhanced liquidity in equity markets supported by lower int=
erest rates and increased global participation. We will continue to support=
 clients with an integrated and enhanced coverage model, ongoing resource e=
fficiency, expanded digital integration and rigorous risk management strate=
gies. </div></div><div style=3D"text-indent: 4%; font-family: arial; font-s=
