<div style=3D"display:inline;">BMO=E2=80=99s overall risk profile can be im=
pacted by evolving internal and external events. These events have the pote=
ntial to affect our business and our operational and financial results. Our=
 risk management life cycle is a continuous process designed to identify, a=
ssess, manage, monitor and report on risks arising from these events. These=
 event-related risks are raised for discussion with the Board of Directors,=
 senior management and business leaders at several forums, incorporating bo=
th <div style=3D"white-space: nowrap; letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display=
:inline;">bottom-up</div> and <div style=3D"white-space: nowrap; letter-spa=
cing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">top-down</div> approaches. Risks are e=
xamined and assessed by scenario analysis. Our exposure to certain events i=
s addressed through action plans developed based on these risk assessments.=
 </div></div> <div style=3D"text-indent: 4%; font-family: arial; font-size:=
 8pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"display:inline;">=
<div style=3D"font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; letter-spacing: 0px; top:=
 0px;display:inline;">The following risks are considered to have the potent=
ial to materially impact BMO=E2=80=99s financial results, operational effic=
iency, strategic direction or&nbsp;reputation. </div></div></div> <div styl=
e=3D"font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 0p=
