 font-size: 8pt; letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">Governance =
of the stress testing framework resides with senior management, including t=
he Enterprise Stress Testing Committee. This committee comprises business, =
risk and finance executives, and is accountable for reviewing and challengi=
ng enterprise-wide scenarios and stress test results. Stress testing and en=
terprise-wide scenarios associated with the ICAAP, including recommendation=
s for actions that the enterprise could take in order to manage the impact =
of a stress event, are established by senior management and presented to th=
e Board of Directors. Oversight and governance of the stress testing associ=
ated with the Horizontal Capital Review (HCR), which is a U.S. regulatory r=
equirement for BMO Financial Corp. (BFC), are exercised at the BFC level by=
 its Board of Directors through its Risk Oversight and Capital Committee. <=
