 margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"color: rgb(34, 92, 171=
); letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">Credit valuation adjustme=
nts (CVA) are fair value adjustments to capture counterparty credit risk in=
 our derivative valuations. CVA profit and loss (P&amp;L) is recognized dai=
ly and provides a mitigant to the loss from a counterparty default by recog=
nizing the expected credit loss given the counterparty=E2=80=99s probabilit=
y of default, as well as our credit exposure. The risks that arise from CVA=
 are subject to our risk governance framework and are actively monitored by=
 a business unit reporting to trading management that has been designated t=
o manage CVA P&amp;L for the bank. Market hedging is performed to manage CV=
A risks. This activity is subject to the bank=E2=80=99s risk control framew=
ork in order to manage the effectiveness of hedges, and to provide independ=
ent review and oversight. The bank calculates CVA capital using both the st=
andardized and basic approach methodologies for CVA. </div></div> </ix:cont=
