nt-family:arial">BMO=E2=80=99s loan book continues to be well-diversified b=
y industry and geographic region. Gross loans and acceptances increased $14=
.1&nbsp;billion or&nbsp;2% from the prior year to&nbsp;$682.7&nbsp;billion =
as at October&nbsp;31, 2024. The geographic mix of BMO=E2=80=99s Canadian a=
nd U.S. portfolios represented&nbsp;57.5% and&nbsp;40.7% of total loans, re=
spectively, compared with&nbsp;55.9% and&nbsp;42.4% in the prior year. The =
loan portfolio is well-diversified, with the consumer loan portfolio repres=
enting&nbsp;43.6% of the total portfolio, a slight decrease from&nbsp;43.9%=
 in the prior year, and business and government loans representing&nbsp;56.=
4% of the total portfolio, a slight increase from&nbsp;56.1% in the prior y=
