><div style=3D"letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;"><div style=3D=
"font-weight:bold;display:inline;">Structural Market Risk Governance </div>=
</div></div></div> <div style=3D"font-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; margin=
-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"color: rgb(34, 92, 171); lett=
er-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">BMO=E2=80=99s Corporate Treasury=
 group is responsible for the ongoing management of structural market risk =
across the enterprise, with independent oversight provided by the Market Ri=
sk group. In addition to the limits approved by our Board of Directors on e=
arnings at risk and the sensitivity of&nbsp;economic value to changes in in=
terest rates, more granular management limits are in place to guide the dai=
ly management of this risk. </div></div> <div style=3D"text-indent: 4%; fon=
t-family: arial; font-size: 8pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><div=
 style=3D"color: rgb(34, 92, 171); letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:in=
line;">The RRC oversees structural market risk management, regularly review=
s structural market risk positions and annually approves the structural&nbs=
p;market risk plan and limits. The RMC and Asset Liability Committee (ALCO)=
 provide ongoing senior management oversight of risk positions and related =
activities. </div></div> <div style=3D"font-family: arial; font-size: 10pt;=
 margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><div style=3D"color: rgb(34, 92, 171=
